### Part 4 — The “deep retrieval era”: sequence models, semantics & embeddings

Now we enter the wave that you listed:

• **Sequence models (RNNs, GRUs, Transformers)**  
• **HSTU, TIGER, etc.** (these are advanced architectures focusing on user behavior modeling, long-term dependencies, better embeddings)

• **Semantic IDs**  
A clever trick from Alibaba and others:  
_turn sparse IDs into dense learnable tokens that capture behavior meaning_  
instead of relying on category or one-hot IDs.

• **Knowledge graphs**  
Used to inject structured relationships (e.g., “this movie shares actors, themes, genres”).  
Helps cold start and diversity.

All of these together form what people call **“representation-rich recommendation.”**

